    "blurb": "The performance offers a laid‑back mood, running through early Dead staples like Hard To Handle, Dire Wolf and a double Good Lovin' sandwich. The soundboard capture is clean, yet the band never hits the high‑water marks of their peak era.",
    "review": "On October 26, 1969 at Winterland Arena the Grateful Dead presented a modest, mood‑focused set that leans heavily on familiar early‑Dead material. While the soundboard recording (gd69-10-26.sbd.fink.9509.sbeok.shnf) is praised for its clarity and lack of technical flaws, listeners note that the band stays in a relaxed groove rather than soaring to the heights seen later in ’70. Jerry’s brief onstage banter about a “long, weird weekend” offers a glimpse of his personality, but there are no standout solos or improvisational peaks. The set rolls through classics—Hard To Handle, Cold Rain And Snow, Dire Wolf, Casey Jones—and includes a fun Good Lovin' sandwich bookended by drums, followed by the upbeat China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider transition, all delivered with solid, if not spectacular, playing.",
